
  [1m3. Wiring and data flow[0m

  - [38;5;153mindex.html[39m: add [38;5;153m<script src="settings.js"></script>[39m immediately [1mbefore[0m the existing [38;5;153mapp.js[39m tag. Order matters;
    [38;5;153mapp.js[39m reads the global at load time.
  - [38;5;153mapp.js[39m line 2 becomes [38;5;153mconst API_ENDPOINT = AppSettings.apiBaseUrl + "/login";[39m — same name, same usage, now derived.
    Nothing else in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m changes.
  - No guard if [38;5;153msettings.js[39m fails to load: [38;5;153mapp.js[39m throws on the missing global. That's deliberate — a loud failure beats
    silently posting credentials at a default host.

  [1m4. Placeholders I'm flagging, not inventing[0m

  Three values go into the spec as [38;5;153mAssumption: … validate via …[39m, not as facts: the staging hostname, the staging base
  URL, and the dev port ([38;5;153mlocalhost:3000[39m is a guess). Production keeps its known value.

  [1m5. Testing[0m

  [38;5;153mdetectEnvironment(hostname)[39m is a pure string-to-string function and the only real logic here — it's worth a handful of
  cases (each dev hostname, staging, unknown → production). But this repo has [1mno tooling at all[0m today: no linter, no
  formatter, no test runner, no dependencies, no [38;5;153mscripts[39m in [38;5;153mpackage.json[39m. So before I write the spec:
